+# Question to Raspberry Pi Ltd on Compute Module 5's radio approval (prepared by the session; sent only by the owner)
+
+Prepared 27 September 2026 (MESHSAT-1357, the layer 3 closer) for registry open item "Raspberry Pi's written position
+on the CM5 radio approval" (CON-011). The session contacts nobody outside; the owner decides whether and when to send
+it. Nothing on the kit changes with the answer: until one is held, no document claims that the module's approval holds
+through the path below.
+
+**To:** Raspberry Pi Ltd, compliance or applications support (the address the owner uses for Compute Module questions).
+
+**Subject:** Compute Module 5 wireless: approval with the Raspberry Pi Antenna Kit through an extended passive path
+
+Dear Raspberry Pi team,
+
+We are designing a prototype carrier for three Compute Module 5 modules (the wireless variant) inside a sealed
+portable case. It is a non-commercial prototype intended for licensed radio amateurs in the Netherlands and the EU;
+nothing has been built or placed on the market. The CM5 datasheet (section 4.1.2 and its antenna note) says that Raspberry Pi
+supports approval only with the Raspberry Pi Antenna Kit (YH2400-5800-SMA-108) and that another antenna needs its own
+approval.
+
+We intend to use the Antenna Kit's own antenna and its U.FL to SMA lead on one module, with the module set to its
+external antenna (dtparam=ant2). Between the lead's SMA end and the antenna there would be a further passive path
+inside the case: a blind-mate RF connector pair, about 200 mm of 50 ohm coaxial cable and a gas-discharge surge
+arrestor used as the wall bulkhead (PolyPhaser GTH-SFF-AL), with the antenna screwed onto the arrestor outside the
+case. The path has no active part and only adds loss; we will measure that loss at 2.4 and 5 GHz on the prototype.
+The other two modules would keep their radios disabled, or use their on-board antenna (dtparam=ant1) if the first
+module fails.
+
+Our questions:
+
+1. Does the module's approval with the Antenna Kit remain valid when the Antenna Kit's antenna is reached through such
+   a passive path that adds only loss, or does any intermediate connector or cable require a separate approval?
+2. If it does not remain valid, is there a maximum added length, a connector type or a loss range within which it
+   does, or an approved extension you can name?
+3. Are there conditions on using the on-board antenna when the module sits on a carrier inside a closed case with an
+   aluminium plate above it, beyond the clearance guidance of section 4.1.2?
+
+Thank you for your time. We will record your answer, with its date, in our design record.
+
+Kind regards,
+
+(the owner's name and contact)
