+# Review B, layer 3 (requirements with verification): the brief for the fresh reviewer (AI review)
+
+Give this to ONE reviewer (a session or a person) that did not write or assemble the requirements registry, its trace
+page or the test plan's requirement trace, and has not seen the sessions that did. It is an AI review and its record
+must say so; it is never a qualified review and never stands in for one. Definition: the registry's session choice on
+Review B (the layer 3 closer's, placeholder `@SC:reviewb@`) and open item "Review B held" (placeholder `@S:reviewb@`).
+No record of this tree requires a qualified review of the requirements (owner ruling D-09's routes cover the battery,
+security, EMC, power and high-speed design).
+
+## Inputs
+
+- The repository at ONE pinned commit: the integration commit that ran `drafts/hc3/apply_registry.py` of fnd/hc3 and
+  re-rendered `v2/docs/REQUIREMENTS-TRACE.md`. Write its hash at the top of the record and read nothing from any other
+  revision.
+- Under review: `v2/ecad/tools/pcb_requirements.yaml` (the registry), `v2/docs/REQUIREMENTS-TRACE.md` (its generated
+  page), `v2/docs/TEST-PLAN.md` (its Purpose and Verifies columns and section 4's trace).
+- The criteria: `v2/docs/reviews/2026-09-27-handover-execution-prompt.md`, section 3 (the layer 3 row) and section 2
+  (what COMPLETE means; nothing lowered, no function dropped, no protection weakened, no scope narrowed to close an
+  item; a feasibility bound that includes failure stays open where the current stage's decision depends on it).
+- The sources the records cite: `v2/docs/CONOPS.md` (section 2 is the needs table the registry pins),
+  `v2/docs/OPERATING-ENVELOPE.md`, `v2/docs/PANEL.md`, `v2/docs/ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md`, `v2/docs/feasibility/`,
+  `v2/ecad/tools/pcb_rules.yaml`, `pcb_decisions.yaml`, `pcb_interfaces.yaml`, `v2/vendor/` (the standards and data the
+  new pass lines rest on: `standards/erc-rec-74-01-2022-05.md`, `standards/mil-std-461g-requirement-matrix.md`,
+  `standards/mil-std-810h-method-516-8.md`, `solar/pvgis-leiden-monthly-2015-2020.json`, `battery/samsung-35e-orbtronic.pdf`,
+  `limesdr/myriadrf-limesdr-mini-2-0-page-20260925.html`).
+- The tools: `python3 v2/ecad/tools/rules_lib.py requirements` (0 errors expected), `python3 v2/ecad/tools/rules_render.py
+  --requirements --check` (current expected), `python3 v2/ecad/tools/tests/run.py requirement`. Their passing is a
+  supporting check, not the review.
+
+## What to determine, each PASS or a FINDING (blocking or minor), with the record id or file and line
+
+1. Every record traces to a need of CONOPS section 2, and the pin (`needs_document_sha256`) is the pinned commit's CONOPS.
+2. Every record is source-linked, and a sample of at least twenty file:line citations, drawn across records, opens at the
+   pinned commit on the text the record relies on (`sources_read_at` names the commit the citations were read at).
+3. Every requirement's acceptance is measurable: the TBD list is empty, no core BLOCKER's pass line carries a hedged or
+   PROVISIONAL number, and every number in a pass line has a source you can open. Check the retyped records by name
+   (REQ-003, REQ-004, REQ-014, REQ-016 and its M1 balance record, REQ-018, REQ-025, REQ-028, REQ-030, REQ-033, REQ-034,
+   REQ-040 to REQ-043, REQ-052, REQ-058, REQ-059, REQ-061, REQ-063, REQ-069, ASM-002, ASM-005, CON-011, CON-013): did any
+   retype LOWER a requirement, drop a function, weaken a protection or narrow a scope to close an item? Say so for each
+   one you judge that way.
+4. Applicability (prototype 1 core or deferred, with its basis) and allocation are on every record; a deferral taken by
+   the session names its choice and reason.
+5. Verification method and phase are on every record, and no record's check needs a later stage's product (REQ-048's
+   old cycle is gone; FEA stages pass the validator's rule).
+6. Contradictions: every open conflict (CFL) is stated with what resolves it; every resolved one either reads PASS on
+   its corrected sources or says why not. Name any contradiction you find between the registry, CONOPS, the envelope and
+   TEST-PLAN that no record carries.
+7. Needs, design choices, assumptions and historical decisions are kept apart; session choices carry authority SESSION
+   and are never presented as the owner's; owner rulings are quoted as ruled (D-06 without D-08; `public-docs`).
+8. Every open item that is a requirement limit is carried by a record; S-items that are design work name the layer
+   they belong to.
+9. Every BLOCKER or MUST_JUSTIFY rule of `pcb_rules.yaml` has a parent record (the page's "Rules to requirements").
+10. TEST-PLAN traces every test to a requirement and states its purpose (REQ-050).
+11. The exposures are stated: which requirement text FEA-003 and FEA-004 would reopen if they close in failure, and the
+    M1 balance record's failing desk reading with its layer-4 item.
+12. The blocked questions of layer 3 (`drafts/hc3/blocked-questions-layer-3.md` of fnd/hc3: the pack's transport
+    classification, the CM5 approval position, the solar path against M1 and the owner's M1 duration being a session
+    planning value, the shared elements, the hydrogen part, the grounding strategy, and CFL-017, the kit with its own
+    pack at D-02a's margins) are stated exactly, each with why layer 3 can or cannot close without it. Judge CFL-017
+    in particular: its three exits (a measured pack arrangement, cells rated beyond +60 C, which reopens D-06, or the
+    owner's reading of D-02a) are none of them the session's to take at desk.
+13. The trace page is generated, current and carries no unqualified claim; no em dashes; prototype framing throughout.
+14. The readings the apply script re-bound at integration (each carries an evidence line saying "re-read at the
+    handover integration" or "read at integration by the layer-3 closer's apply script"): for CFL-001, CFL-016, REQ-072,
+    REQ-050, CFL-007, CFL-008 and CFL-009, open the pinned files and confirm the text each line says it rests on is
+    there and says what the reading needs.
+15. The reverse trace, as a question for the test plan's owner rather than REQ-050's acceptance: which records whose
+    verification method includes PROTOTYPE_MEASUREMENT have no test that names them, in TEST-PLAN or in a page it
+    points to (`ARCH-PCB-B-IOHA.md` section 13's A1 to A14, `feasibility/EMCON.md` section 6, `feasibility/ZEROIZE.md`
+    section 5, `CASE-MARGINS.md`'s fit checks)? On the closer's integration simulation 42 such records were not named
+    anywhere in TEST-PLAN; list the ones no page plans a test for.
+
+## The record
+
+Write `v2/docs/reviews/REVIEW-B-LAYER-3-<YYYY-MM-DD>.md` (the form of layers 1 and 2's Review A records), first line
+"AI review (not a qualified review)", then
+the reviewer, the pinned commit, a table of the fifteen checks (PASS or FINDING), and each finding with its record id
+or file and line, what is wrong, what would fix it, and blocking or minor. Do not edit the files under review. After
+the fixes, the same reviewer re-checks the blocking findings once; after two unsuccessful passes on the same finding
+the method changes (handover prompt section 4). When a record with no open blocking finding is filed, the registry's
+`baseline_state` becomes `BASELINED_<commit>` at that commit, the open item "Review B held" moves to the closed items
+with that commit, and layer 3's row in `v2/docs/handover/LAYER-STATUS.md` becomes COMPLETE.
